<blockquote>
On the Lighter Side: Munchkin Powergamer Convention<br />
Written by <a href="mailto:mayhem@conclaveofguilds.com">Mayhem</a><br />
<br />
Since this column focuses simply on humor, it's not for everyone.  Some
readers don't really look to be amused because they're too concerned with
finding the information they want about the games they play to be bothered
by such things.  Humor is also a personal thing, so not everyone finds the
same things funny.  I write things I find amusing, and if someone else does
that's just a bonus. Hopefully you'll find something to enjoy in this
article.  First my disclaimer: any resemblance of these fictional characters
to actual persons living or dead is intentional.  But they're only
archetypical individuals with exaggerated (in some ways at least)
characteristics anyway, so don't take it personally.<br />
<br />
Our scene: midnight at the "MMORPG Roundtable Discussion" deep in the
hallowed halls of the summer 2003 "Munchkin Powergamer Convention" . . . a.k.a. the basement of the Miller home in Podunk, middle America.<br />
<br />
[The members of the discussion filter back in from the pause, there is much
bragging and shoving as seats are taken once again.]<br />
<br />
Sturgg (Foesmiter - Chairman of the Discussion and UO Grandmaster Warrior):
Ok, everyone have their Mountain Dew, Jolt, Vivarin, candy bars and
cheetos?<br />
<br />
Gundar (Slayerofall - Shadowbane Fanboy): The vending machine ran out of
Skittles.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Oh, uh, ok, we need a volunteer to scout for convenience stores.<br
/>
<br />
Hakkor (Slash - AC2 Enthusiast)12-Year-Old-Brother-and-Whipping-Boy): I'll
go.  I don't want Gundar to put me in the closet again anyway.<br />
<br />
Gundar: You're getting smarter all the time.<br />
<br />
Hakkor: [muttering] Just wait until I'm bigger, lamer.<br />
<br />
[Orders are taken, money is organized, ten minutes pass and Hakkor goes in
search of a Circle-K.]<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Now, are we ready?  Cool.  Before the break we were discussing
Horizons, but the agenda calls for an open discussion of Everquest II, lead
by our "point-man", Shrub Roots.<br />
<br />
Shrub (Roots - EQ Epic Halfling Druid): Well, looks like the game is still
on schedule, the devs say Q4, and the resellers say November.<br />
<br />
Grog (Guzzler - EQ Epic Troll Warrior): We've all heard that one before.<br
/>
Shrub: Shut up Mel, I'm givin' this report.  Now, the word on the street is
that there's going to be a Beta coming up in August.  Unconfirmed, but if
you read between the lines everyone agrees.<br />
<br />
Shara (Silverlight - EQ Epic High Elf Mage): Nobody agrees, I've read those
polls.<br />
<br />
Gundar: I don't read if I can help it.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Ok, my character is short but I'm bigger than everyone but Shara
so-<br />
<br />
Shara: [cutting Shrub off] Hey! I'm a beautiful high elf maiden with a
flaming pet, besides, I have "big bones" . . .
<br />
Shrub: Right, so *ANYWAY* there's bound to be a Beta soon.  We need to get
coordinated in order to get in.  Eveyone should apply from multiple
computers with multiple sets of personal details.  If we can each manage
five sets of applications, we should get enough Beta accounts to set up a
rotation schedule.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Does it have PvP?<br />
<br />
Shrub: There will be servers that-<br />
<br />
Gundar: [cutting Shrub off] Does the Beta have PvP?
<br />
Shrub: Probably duelling and arenas but-<br />
<br />
Gundar: [cutting Shrub off] I'm not gonna log in unless there's PvP you
know.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Did you not get in enough UT today or something?  How do you expect
to have the skills to kill anyone if you don't practice, idiot?<br />
<br />
Gundar: Fine, but if it sucks I'm just going to play Shadowbane.<br />
<br />
Shrub: So, that's how we'll flood the Beta apps.  Now, for rotations, we'll
be setting up a schedule so that everyone has the maximum possible window.
Remember that when we play we need to find the best spots for levelling, not
to mention any, heh, "anomalous" areas.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Should you or any member of your team be captured, the agency will
have no choice but to disavow your activities.<br />
<br />
Grog: Huh?<br />
<br />
Strugg: Come on!  Have you been living in a cave?<br />
<br />
Grog: My parents' basement is like a cave . . . <br />
<br />
Shrub: Mission Impossible, duh.  He's saying that you need to not get caught
exploiting, or if you do, make sure you tell them you were "gathering data
for a bug report" or some such crap.  But it's best to not get caught and
hope they don't fix the exploit until after we get to use it.<br />
<br />
Grog: Is that that movie with the guy from Top Gun?  Tom Cruise?<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Yeah, I thought the first one was good, but man John Woo is
awesome.<br />
<br />
Grog: Oh yeah, and the face peeling!<br />
<br />
Shrub: Ok, enough with the "Mission Unwatchable" crap!  Just remember to
make all your reports to the forums, and don't leave a lame post like Iggy
did during the AO Beta.<br />
<br />
Forst (Fyre - EQ Epic Human Wizard): How many damn times do I need to say
sorry?  I hadn't slept in two days and I was going to my grandmother's for a
week!<br />
<br />
Grog: Yeah, but dude, what did you say again?  All I remember is that Shara
spent the next three days hunting for some kind of secret spot to stand in
which gave you good missions every time.<br />
<br />
Shara: I spent 20 hours logged on trying to figure out an exploit that
didn't exist because of that.  I could have been raiding Guk.  Three robes
dropped during that raid.  THREE.<br />
<br />
Forst: I said I was sorry.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Like I said, post all the important things, but make sure you've
slept or used a spell-checker or don't have your head stuck in a drawer or
something.<br />
<br />
Shara: The next person one of you boys who wastes my time like that is going
to get a nasty suprise.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Oh crap, you'll kiss us?<br />
<br />
[Gundar is hit in the face by a rain of peanut M&Ms.]
<br />
Shrub: Ok already! Let's talk goals!  One: find the good hunting spots, Two:
discover if they've nerfed druids-<br />
<br />
Sturgg: [cutting Shrub off] Nobody cares about druids but you.  Are you
going to cry if you have to group to play the game effectively?<br />
<br />
Shrub: I do group!<br />
<br />
Grog: Yeah, when we raid somewhere that you want gear from that nobody will
sell you.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Druids like solitude!< br/>
<br />
Shara: Druids like to abuse "area" spells.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Whatever, I just think that some provisions for soloers are a good
plan, that's all.  I don't really like the talk I'm hearing of groups being
far more effective than soloing.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Better pray your little druids get better heals, because I'm
thinking I might want someone competent watching my skin.<br />
<br />
Shrub: What do you know?  You stopped playing to play inferior games with
your pet, err *brother* a year ago.<br />
<br />
Shara: I prefer my pets the be part of the game.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Good thing too, we don't want to be your pets!<br />
<br />
Shara: You're such a sucker Gundar, give me one reason I shouldn't beat you
down right now!
<br />
Grog: You two need to get a room and work it out.<br />
<br />
Forst: Yeah, too much S E X A U L tension.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Sexaul?  Is that like a U-Haul with benefits?<br />
<br />
Forst: Huh? S E X - uh, sorry, yeah - U A L tension.<br />
<br />
[Hakkor returns with "food".]<br />
<br />
Hakkor: That trick doesn't work any more.  I learned how to spell a long
time ago.  Who has sexual tension?<br />
<br />
Gundar: Not me!<br />
<br />
Hakkor: Wrong answer, I heard mom and dad reaming you about the Visa
bill.<br />
<br />
Gundar: You little-<br />
<br />
Shrub: [cutting Gundar off] Ok, enough, kill him when we're done.<br />
<br />
Shara: [making certain obvious hand motions] Oooo, oooo, you hot bunch of
pixels.<br />
<br />
Shrub: I wouldn't talk if I were you. I've never seen more posters of
Harrison Ford on one wall in my life than I did in your room. [a silent
moment passes] Now, if we're going to be first to hit 100th level after
release-<br />
<br />
Hakkor: [cutting Shrub off] It only goes to 100?<br />
<br />
Gundar: It goes all the way to 100?<br />
<br />
Shrub: Yes, 100.  It's supposed to take just as long to get to 100 as it did
to 50 originally.  So we have a month, max.  We're not the only ones who
want to max out fast, and you better believe that if some other guild
manages it, we're not going to get the front page of Stratics. So this time
we're going to shoot for 24 hour manning on at least six characters.  Right
now we don't know what six, but we need to balance them against each
other.<br />
<br />
Forst: Warrior, Wizard, Cleric, Rogue, Bard, Enchanter, duh.<br />
<br />
Shrub: We don't even know what classes will exist, idiot!<br />
<br />
Shara: Mages are better than Wizards anyway.  I hear that teleport spells
will be weak.<br />
<br />
Forst: Oh, and you think they're giving evacs to Mages?<br />
<br />
Shrub: We also don't know the spell lists!  It's not the same game!<br />
<br />
Shara: Wizards will always be less useful than Mages, even if it isn't the
same game.<br />
<br />
Hakkor: Why can't we all just play AC2?<br />
<br />
[Various "food", much of which was only recently acquired, hits Hakkor.]<br
/>
<br />
Shrub: So, the sign-up sheet will be available at least two weeks before we
expect the game to release, but if there's an emergency everyone will just
have to rearrange to fit into a slot.<br />
<br />
Forst: I'm going to Bermuda in November.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Why?<br />
<br />
Forst: My sister is getting married.<br />
<br />
Shara: Just wait, the day before he leave there will be somee crap in the
forums about a leprechaun and unlimited gold to be had.  Then I'll waste
three days trying to find it.<br />
<br />
Gundar: I could help you look . . .<br />
<br />
Shrub: Isn't that sweet.  Ok, Forst, if you go on vacation you're gonna miss
a spot on the rotation, and it might be permanent.  So if that happens,
you're "on-call" as soon as you get back in case someone can't log in.<br />
<br />
Forst: Ah crap, come on, I'm ALWAYS on-call.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: You haven't been on-call since we started exploring Velious.<br />
<br />
Forst: I almost went snow-blind after the first week.  Yigri called me at
3am on night because Tullik got sick and they needed me to sign on!  I was
late for work at least five times that month alone!<br />
<br />
Shrub: Nobody told you to go to your sister's wedding in Bermuda.<br />
<br />
Forst: BS!  My *parents* told me.<br />
<br />
Gundar: You think there's going to be a lot of "thong" goin' on down
there?<br />
<br />
Shara: Pig.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Harpy.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Ok, enough already.  I'll make sure to post the vital points on the
forums for the rest of the guys.  But remember, we're gonna be number one.
No more "Afterlife" or "Fires of Heaven" in the news all the time.  No,
it's gonna be us.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Oh yeah, the poll is gonna close about the new guild name.
Actually, I'm tired of resetting it, so can you idiots stop purging your
cookies and IP-spoofing?  Let's make this last time official, or I'm gonna
make it an open ballot.<br />
<br />
Hakkor: Huh?  What do you mean?<br />
<br />
Gundar: He means everyone is gonna know you're the one who voted 384 times
for "Hakkor's Heros", as if we couldn't have guessed.<br />
<br />
Hakkor: Right, but I only found all those redirectors because of your
attempts to get "The Legions of Shara" elected!<br />
<br />
Shara: I *wondered* where all those votes came from!<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Anyway, I'll pick a name if we can't have a straight vote.  See how
you like being a member of the "Knights of the Pansy" guild!<br />
<br />
Forst: "Arcane Order" is really the best of them all.<br />
<br />
Shrub: "Forces of Nature" is, and you all know it.<br />
Forst: If it didn't work out for Ben Afleck, it's not going to work for
us.<br />
<br />
Shara: I thought it was really a romantic movie!<br />
<br />
Gundar: Oooo, ooo, Ben, I love you Ben!<br />
<br />
Hakkor: You're just jealous, Steve.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Anyway, before this degenerates into Hakkor being stuffed behind the
furnace again, I think we've concluded the evening's agenda, at least as far
as EQ2.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: Yeah, that's it.  Let's get out of here.<br />
<br />
Gundar: Be quiet going out, the door is still squeaky and my mom is a light
sleeper.<br />
<br />
Hakkor: And he's still in trouble for the "Exclusive Services" charges on
the card!<br />
<br />
[Chaos erupts, Hakkor flees the room just ahead of a deluge of Mountain Dew.
The weary gamers being to shuffle out.]
<br />
Gundar: Uh, Shara, I have "Patriot Games" on DVD, you know, if you wanna
watch it.<br />
<br />
Shara: I have that one too, but on video.<br />
<br />
Gundar: No, I mean you can hang out and watch it, I don't have to do
anything until late tomorrow, so I wouldn't mind.  You know, the sound is
really good on my system.<br />
<br />
Shara: Yeah, ok, I've got a raid tomorrow morning with "The Bloodcult" . . .
but I don't mind missing it since I'm just backing them up as a favor
anyway.<br />
<br />
Shrub: Ahem, uh, good night.<br />
<br />
Gundar and Shara: Oh, good night guys!<br />
<br />
Forst: [nodding sagely] Uh-huh.<br />
<br />
Sturgg: [fading away up the stairs] Good day Mr. Hunt, your mission should
you choose to . . .<br />
<br />
Shrub: [in the distance] I still think it's "shi mer a", not "kai mer a" . .
.<br />
<br />
Shara: You kinda look like Harrison Ford, like in "Star Wars".<br />
<br />
Gundar: Wanna see my DVDs?<br />
<br />
Thus we leave our look at the sordid secret meetings of the elite powergamer
crew.  Will the guild be named after a flower?  Will Shara put Gundar in a
headlock for "getting funny" during "K-19", or will it blossom into true
geek love?  Do we care?  Will there even be a next time?  To find out, check
back here at Conclave of Guilds.<br />
<br />
</blockquote>
